+---
+
+## Detailed Condition Notes
+
+1. **Token Scope Restriction:** Scoped MCP Agents can only exercise capabilities explicitly included in their minted token scopes (`read:issues`, `write:issues`, `read:docs`, `write:docs`, `admin`, etc.). Unscoped tools are rejected with `403 FORBIDDEN`.
+2. **Explicit Project Membership / ACL Share:** Guests and Viewers cannot see private project entities unless explicitly added to the project role bindings or granted a specific `ALLOW` entry in `resource_acl_entries`.
+3. **Absolute DENY Precedence:** If an explicit `DENY` entry exists for a principal on an object (or inherited group), effective capability bitmasks collapse immediately (`allow & (~deny)`). Even Workspace Admins cannot view or manage objects guarded by an explicit `DENY`.
+4. **Ownership Share Delegation:** Standard Members can only share objects they originally authored, provided project policy permits user-level ACL delegation.
+5. **Admin Approval Gate:** Custom fields and scripts can only be defined by administrators. Executing a script with Workspace or Server token escalation requires cryptographic approval from an administrator of that tier.
+6. **Author Deletion Scope:** Members may soft-delete their own drafts, comments, and un-assigned stickies if granted DELETE capability mask. Project-wide item soft-deletion requires Project Admin.
+7. **Project Scope Isolation:** Project Admins in the Trash Studio can only view and restore items belonging to projects where they hold explicit `PROJECT_ADMIN` authority.
+8. **Fresh AAL2 Step-Up Requirement:** All administrative endpoints (`/api/v1/admin/*`, retention settings, user provisioning, trash operations, key minting) enforce `Depends(require_admin_aal2)`. The session must have verified MFA within the last 900 seconds (`aal2_verified_at <= 900s`).
+9. **Daemon Background Job Authority:** The trash purge runner executes with dedicated system worker identity and sweeps expired entities strictly past their per-workspace `trash_retention_days` threshold.
+10. **2-Stage Destructive Confirmation:** Permanent purge is exclusively gated to `SERVER_ADMIN` + fresh AAL2. It requires `POST /api/v1/admin/destructive:request` to compute blast radius and mint an ephemeral HMAC `confirmation_token` + `blast_hash`, followed by `POST /api/v1/admin/destructive:execute` with a mandatory human reason (10 to 500 characters).
+11. **Project-Level Role Delegation:** Project Admins may manage role bindings within their designated project only. They cannot elevate users to Workspace Admin or Server Admin.
+12. **Cryptographic Immutability:** Audit ledger tables (`activity_ledger`) have no `UPDATE` or `DELETE` grants for any database role (including `kanban_app` and `kanban_migrator`). Triggers prevent tampering.
+
+---
+
+## Architectural Security Invariants
+
+- **Hostile Wire Invariant:** Every input is validated with strict Pydantic schemas and UTF-8 surrogate checks. Cleartext transmission of tokens is prohibited.
+- **Walled Component Garden:** Row-Level Security (`FORCE ROW LEVEL SECURITY`) is always active on all database sessions. Dropping session authorization to unprivileged users is mandatory in application flows.
+- **Volatile State Sanitization:** Ephemeral tokens and secrets exist only in memory during execution and are erased immediately after verification.
+- **Supply Chain Paranoia:** Zero external cloud runtime dependencies for core authentication, authorization, or search.
